column477:
* Test word: {{internationalization}}
* Optional hyphen insertion point: after {{inter}} (between {{inter}} and {{nationalization}})
* Preceding filler text: enough text to push {{internationalization}} close to a line-break point when the window is resized

* Paragraph 1: {{This is the first paragraph.}}
* Paragraph 2: {{This is the second paragraph.}}
* Paragraph spacing after: 12 pt

* Line 1: {{First line of the paragraph.}}
* Line 2 (soft return — same paragraph): {{Second line, same paragraph.}}
* Line 3 (new paragraph): {{This is a new paragraph.}}
* Paragraph spacing after: 12 pt

column479:
* Open a blank document in Editor.
* Set paragraph spacing to 12 pt after paragraph.
* Type {{First line of the paragraph.}}
* Press Shift+Enter.
* Observe whether the cursor moves to the next line without creating a new paragraph.
* Type {{Second line, same paragraph.}}
* Press Enter.
* Type {{This is a new paragraph.}}
* Observe spacing between all three lines. The 12 pt spacing must appear only between {{Second line, same paragraph.}} and {{This is a new paragraph.}} — not between lines 1 and 2.
* With formatting marks visible, confirm a ↵ symbol appears after line 1 and a ¶ symbol appears after line 2.

column477:
* Paragraph before break: {{End of section one.}}
* Paragraph after break: {{Start of section two.}}
* Current page number at insertion point: even (e.g., page 2)

* Paragraph before break: {{End of section one.}}
* Paragraph after break: {{Start of section two.}}
* Current page number at insertion point: odd (e.g., page 1)

* Section start: {{New Page}}
* Header from edge: {{0.5"}}
* Footer from edge: {{0.5"}}
* Vertical alignment: {{Center}}

* Document text containing at least two instances of: {{"fox"}}
* Search term: {{"fox"}}
* Replacement term: {{"cat"}}

column404:
Each casing option must transform the selected text as follows, consistent with Word Desktop behavior:

* {{UPPERCASE}} → {{"THE QUICK BROWN FOX JUMPS OVER THE LAZY DOG"}}
* {{lowercase}} → {{"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"}}
* {{Title Case}} → {{"The Quick Brown Fox Jumps Over The Lazy Dog"}}
* {{Sentence case}} → {{"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"}}
* {{tOGGLE cASE}} → {{"tHE qUICK bROWN fOX jUMPS oVER tHE lAZY dOG"}}

column477:
* Sample paragraph: {{"Water chemical formula is H2O and speed of light is 3x10^8 m/s"}}
* Superscript selection: {{"8"}} (in {{10^8}})
* Subscript selection: {{"2"}} (in {{H2O}})

* Sample paragraph: {{"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"}}
* Selected portion: {{"brown fox"}}
* New font size: {{18}}

* Initial text: {{Hello World}}
* Search keyword to type in the font search box: {{Geor}}
* Font to select from the dropdown results: {{Georgia}}

* Paragraph text: {{The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog}}
* Table dimensions: 2 × 2
* Table cell text: {{The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog}}
* Text to select: {{brown fox}} (a partial mid-sentence selection)
* Font to change to: {{Arial}}

* Initial text: {{Hello World}}
* Font to switch to: any font other than Times New Roman (e.g., {{Arial}})
* Follow-up text: {{This is a test}}

* Paragraph text: {{Hello World}}
* Table dimensions: 2 × 2
* Table cell text: {{Hello World}}

h3. 

* Document type: Blank single-page document (repeat on a multi-page document).
* Templates to test one by one from Editor's dropdown:
** {{Blank}}
** {{Blank (Three Columns)}}
** {{Austin}}
** {{Banded}}
* Expected placeholder text per Word's behavior:
** *Blank* → Single centered placeholder: {{[Document Title]}}
** *Blank (Three Columns)* → Three placeholders across the header: {{[Document Title]}} / {{[Document Subtitle]}} / {{[Page Number]}}
** *Austin* → Styled banner with {{[Document Title]}} placeholder and a horizontal rule
** *Banded* → Dark-banded bar with {{[Document Title]}} placeholder text styled in white

* Dialog to test: Find & Replace (Ctrl + H)
* Find field value: {{hello}}
* Replace field value: {{world}}
* These values are entered but the Replace / Replace All button is NOT clicked before the background click is performed.

